            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "madeō, madēre — \"to be soaking wet, to drip\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Post imbrem vestēs viātōrum madent. After the downpour the travellers' clothes are soaking wet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "madeō, madēre, maduī, second conjugation, no supine. Also, in comedy, to be drunk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "madeō is inherited from PIE meh₂d- 'to drip, to ooze' (EtymDB); Lewis & Short compare Greek madaō 'to be moist'."
            }
          ]
        },
